 "description": "\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\tEtymology as Archaeology\n\t\n\nA dataset of words pulled apart — the gap between technical definition and deeper structure.\nEach entry takes a word and traces its etymology, then finds the structural insight hiding in the gap between what the word used to mean and what it means now. The method: etymology → shift → gap → application. The glossary isn't archaeology. It's translation — carrying frozen definitions across into living perception. The door isn't in the dictionary. The door… See the full description on the dataset page: https://huggingface.co/datasets/sdeture/etymology-as-archaeology.",
